  "title": "Gupta Empire",
  "summary": "The Gupta Empire dominated northern India from about 320 CE, when Chandragupta I became its first sovereign ruler. At its height it stretched across northern, central and parts of southern India, with Pataliputra, near modern Patna, as Samudragupta's capital. It is remembered as a Golden Age; Hun invasions ended it, around 550 CE by one reckoning and 500 CE by another.",
